      "math_academy_id": "q-149725",
      "sequence_position": 75,
      "problem": "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}3{a}_{i}(4-{b}_{j})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}=30,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{j}=45.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}3{a}_{i}(4-{b}_{j}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}3{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(4-{b}_{j}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}3{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(4-{b}_{j}) & =(3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}4-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{j}) \\\\  & =(3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i})\\cdot (4{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{j}) \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 30)\\cdot (4\\cdot 12-45) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (48-45) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (3) \\\\  & =270\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
